            <ArticleTitle>[Persisting pain after open articulosynovectomy--gossypiboma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>616-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0029-1185411</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report about a 44-year-old woman who presented at our Orthopaedic Department suffering from persisting pain and a tumor of the right knee after open articulosynovectomy. MRI did not clarify the entity at all. The X-ray examination could identify an inlying compress after a synovectomy in 1999. The intra-articular foreign body could be removed by open revision surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
